    "description": "Henry H001 Traditional Handguards: Laffs Dynamics\n\n3D printed handguards for the Henry Repeating Arms H001 rifle and model variants. (As of 2026, designated the H1) \n\nTwo model variants are available:\n\n *Traditional: A basic diamond checkered pattern.\n\n *Refined: Diamond checkered pattern with double fleur-de-lis emblems, has contoured thumb and finger shelved atop the handguard.\n\n\nCompatible with model lines:\n\nH1 Classic Rifle: H001-22, H001-22M, H001L-22, H001L-22M\n\nH1 Classic Carbine: H001R-22, H001R-22M\n\nH1 Garden Gun: H001GG-22\n\nH1 Classic Youth Model: H001Y-22, H001Y-22M\n\nH1 Mare’s Leg Pistol: H001ML-22, H001ML-22M\n\n\n\nFilament Used: PLA+ (CF-Nylon recommended for long term)\n\nPLA+ Print Settings:\n\nExtruder: 220C \nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .12mm\nWall Thickness: .40mm\nWall Perimeters: 6+\nInfill: 60%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 20%\n\nFor best aesthetic results, print the design vertically. (Rear facet flat on the build plate)\n\n\n\nAccreditations:\n\nNotsogod: Printed both handguard models horizontal and vertical to the 3D printer's Z axis; both in CF-Nylon and PLA+. Took images of the prototype \nprints, and shipped the finished models to the designer. ",
